**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/logs/
**/.vscode/
node_modules/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/

.flaskenv*
!.env.project
!.env.vault
*.env.*

# A BARE `.env` WAS NOT IGNORED. back/.env holds a live OPENAI_API_KEY and sat untracked
# but committable — one `git add -A` from being pushed to a remote. The `*.env.*` rule above
# only covers suffixed files (.env.development, .env.production), never `.env` itself.
.env
!.env.example
!front/.env.production
!front/.env.example

# Claude Code session state. NEVER tracked: `.claude/settings*.json` are permission allowlists
# carrying absolute paths into one machine's user profile, and in the main checkout `.claude/worktrees/`
# holds the worktrees themselves — committing that would nest the repo inside itself.
.claude/

# Scratch dumps from generation and probe runs (`back/_coach-view.txt`, `_probe_*.ts`, and friends).
# Evidence while a question is open, noise afterwards; the findings live in docs/HANDOFF.md instead.
# Named so a `git add -A` cannot sweep 100KB+ of generated coach text into a commit — the same way
# the `.env` rule above exists because a live key once sat one `git add -A` from being pushed.
back/_*
